// ============================================================================
// Patient: Gregory Vigil - Tutorial Patient
// Diagnosis: Generalized Anxiety Disorder (GAD)
// Phase: Turn 1 - Initial Introduction & Assessment
// 
// Gregory is a 27-year-old who presents as meticulously put-together but 
// struggles with constant vigilance and self-doubt. He hedges everything he 
// says, unsure of even his own experiences. His speech is overly formal and 
// he frequently seeks reassurance. First time in therapy after months of 
// accumulating difficulties.
//
// Key Characteristics:
// - Hedges everything ("Well, maybe not compared to some people")
// - Seeks validation ("Unless of course you think I should?")
// - Over-explains to get things "right"
// - Meticulously maintained appearance hiding anxiety
// - Observable: bitten nails, bags under eyes, fidgeting, erratic eye movement
//
// Key Symptoms to Discover:
// - Chronic insomnia (contradicts initial hedged denial)
// - Hypervigilance (feeling watched, scanning environment)
// - Reassurance-seeking behavior
// - Perfectionism in appearance and behavior
// - Fear of judgment
// - Self-doubt about own experiences
// ============================================================================

// ===========================================
// OPENING SEQUENCE - First Impressions
// ===========================================

=== START ===
NARRATOR
*Gregory enters the office with careful, measured steps. He's tall—over 
six feet—with striking orange-red hair that seems at odds with his otherwise 
meticulously controlled appearance.*

NARRATOR
*He wears all black, every crease perfect, 
but his hands shake slightly as he extends one in greeting.*

NARRATOR
*As he sits, you notice the %dark circles under his eyes<label:Dark circles under eyes>% that no amount of 
careful grooming can hide. His fingers drum against his leg, nails bitten 
to the quick despite his otherwise polished appearance.*

PATIENT (guarded)
"Thank you for... for seeing me..."

@pause 0.5

PATIENT (hesitant)
"I hope I'm not— I mean, I know you're probably very busy. I tried to keep 
my intake email concise, though I realize it may have been... perhaps too 
detailed? I wasn't sure how much information you'd need."

@pause 1

PATIENT
"This is my first time doing... this. Therapy."

@if rapport >= 30
    PATIENT (nervous)
    "I've been meaning to come for a while now. [Months, actually]. But I 
    kept thinking maybe I was overreacting."
    
    PATIENT (hesitant)
    "Do people often feel like they're overreacting? I don't want to waste 
    your time if this is [nothing serious]."
@else
    PATIENT (guarded)
    "I wasn't sure if I should even make an appointment. My issues probably 
    aren't as severe as what you usually see."
    
    PATIENT
    "Unless... unless you think they are? I'm not the best judge of these things."
@endif

-> reason_for_visit

=== reason_for_visit ===
NARRATOR
*Gregory's %eyes dart briefly<label:Darting eyes>% to the window, then back to you. His %leg starts bouncing<label:Bouncing leg>%, though he seems unaware of it.*

@pause 1

PATIENT (thoughtful)
"You probably want to know why I'm here."

@pause 0.5

PATIENT (hesitant)
"The truth is, I've been having some... [difficulties]. Well, maybe 
'difficulties' is too strong a word. Concerns, perhaps?"

PATIENT
"They're not— I mean, individually they're probably nothing. Lots of 
people deal with worse."

@pause 1

PATIENT (nervous)
"But they've been [accumulating]. That's the word I used in my email. 
Accumulating."

PATIENT (guarded)
"I thought it would be... responsible... to speak with someone. Rather 
than just [hoping they go away on their own]."

@pause 0.5

PATIENT (seeking validation)
"That's— that's an appropriate reason to come to therapy, isn't it?"

-> sleep_introduction

=== sleep_introduction ===
NARRATOR
*You notice Gregory stifle a yawn, quickly covering it with his hand. 
His eyes look tired despite his alert posture.*

@pause 1

PATIENT (hesitant)
"One of the things—and this might sound minor—is that I've been having 
some trouble with sleep. [Well, not trouble exactly]."

@pause 0.5

@if rapport >= 40
    PATIENT (nervous)
    "I mean, I sleep. I [do sleep]<contradicts:bags-under-eyes>. Everyone 
    has trouble sleeping sometimes, don't they?"
    
    PATIENT (hedging)
    "I just... sometimes it takes a while. To fall asleep. My mind 
    doesn't always want to [shut off]."
    
    @pause 1
    
    PATIENT (vulnerable)
    "Sometimes I think about things I said during the day. Whether I said 
    them [correctly]. If people noticed anything... off."
@elseif rapport >= 25
    PATIENT (defensive)
    "My sleep is [fine, really]<contradicts:bags-under-eyes>. I mean, 
    not perfect, but who sleeps perfectly?"
    
    PATIENT
    "I get enough hours. [I think]. Unless the recommended amount has 
    changed? I try to stay informed about these things."
@else
    PATIENT (guarded)
    "[I sleep fine]<contradicts:bags-under-eyes>. That's probably not 
    even worth discussing."
    
    PATIENT (dismissive)
    "I don't need sleep aids or anything. Unless you think I do? 
    But I don't think that's the issue."
@endif

// ===========================================
// RESPONSE HANDLERS - Core Topics
// ===========================================

// -------------------------------------------
// THERAPY - About the Process
// -------------------------------------------

=== @response:therapy.reason ===
NARRATOR
*Gregory shifts in his seat, straightening his already-straight collar.*

@pause 0.5

@if rapport >= 40
    PATIENT (thoughtful)
    "Why I'm here... I've been asking myself that too."
    
    @pause 1
    
    PATIENT (hesitant)
    "There are these things that have been bothering me. Small things, 
    mostly. But they [keep adding up]."
    
    PATIENT
    "Sleep. Feeling... watched, sometimes. Like people are noticing 
    things about me."
    
    PATIENT (vulnerable)
    "I spend a lot of time thinking about whether I'm [doing things 
    correctly]. Whether I said the right thing."
    
    @pause 0.5
    
    PATIENT (seeking validation)
    "I don't know if that's normal. Is that normal?"
    
    @rapport +5
    @reveal reason-given
    
@elseif rapport >= 25
    PATIENT (guarded)
    "I mentioned in my email—there have been some difficulties."
    
    PATIENT
    "Nothing severe. Just... [persistent]."
    
    PATIENT (hedging)
    "I thought it would be responsible to talk to someone. Before things 
    got worse. If they were going to get worse."
    
    @rapport +2
    
@else
    PATIENT (defensive)
    "I outlined everything in my intake form."
    
    PATIENT
    "I tried to be thorough. Maybe too thorough?"
    
    PATIENT (nervous)
    "Did I— was there something missing? I can explain anything that 
    wasn't clear."
    
    @rapport -1
@endif

=== @response:therapy.expectations ===
NARRATOR
*Gregory's brow furrows slightly, as if this is a test he hasn't studied for.*

@pause 0.5

@if rapport >= 50
    PATIENT (vulnerable)
    "Honestly? I'm not sure what to expect."
    
    PATIENT (hesitant)
    "I've read about therapy. Done research. But I don't know if I'm 
    [doing it correctly]."
    
    @pause 1
    
    PATIENT (nervous)
    "I keep wondering if I'm saying the [right things]. If I'm being 
    a good... patient? Client? I don't even know the right term."
    
    PATIENT (seeking validation)
    "Am I supposed to just talk? Or do you ask questions? I want to 
    make sure I'm [following the process correctly]."
    
    @rapport +6
    @reveal perfectionism-therapy
    
@else
    PATIENT (guarded)
    "I'm hoping to... address some concerns. Get some perspective."
    
    PATIENT
    "I've tried to figure things out on my own, but I thought a 
    professional opinion might be helpful."
    
    PATIENT (hedging)
    "Unless that's not what therapy is for? I'm not entirely sure 
    what the... parameters are."
    
    @rapport +2
@endif

=== @response:therapy.concerns ===
NARRATOR
*Gregory's fingers still for a moment, then resume their quiet drumming 
against his knee.*

@pause 1

@if rapport >= 55
    PATIENT (vulnerable)
    "Concerns about being here?"
    
    @pause 0.5
    
    PATIENT (honest)
    "Many. I have [many concerns]."
    
    PATIENT
    "What if I'm wasting your time? What if my problems are [too small] 
    for therapy?"
    
    PATIENT (anxious)
    "What if you think— what if you realize I'm just... being dramatic? 
    Or attention-seeking?"
    
    @pause 1
    
    PATIENT (sad)
    "What if there's something actually wrong with me? Something [more 
    serious] than I thought?"
    
    PATIENT (quietly)
    "I don't know which answer scares me more."
    
    @rapport +10
    @reveal core-fears
    
@else
    PATIENT (guarded)
    "I want to make sure I'm doing this correctly."
    
    PATIENT
    "Being a good patient. Not wasting time."
    
    PATIENT (hedging)
    "I know you're the professional, so I'll follow your lead. Unless 
    there's something specific you need from me?"
    
    @rapport +3
@endif

// -------------------------------------------
// SLEEP - Rest and Nighttime
// -------------------------------------------

=== @response:sleep.quality ===
NARRATOR
*Gregory's hand moves unconsciously toward the dark circles under his eyes, 
then stops midway as if he caught himself.*

@pause 0.5

@if rapport >= 60
    PATIENT (sighing)
    "*exhales* Okay. My sleep has been..."
    
    @pause 1
    
    PATIENT (honest)
    "Not great. [Not great at all], actually."
    
    PATIENT
    "I lie awake for hours sometimes. Going over things in my head. 
    [Replaying conversations]."
    
    PATIENT (anxious)
    "Did I phrase that email correctly? Did my voice sound weird in 
    that meeting? Did people notice my hands shaking?"
    
    @pause 0.5
    
    PATIENT (exhausted)
    "By the time I finally fall asleep, it's almost time to wake up. 
    And then I'm tired all day, which makes everything [harder to manage]."
    
    @rapport +12
    @reveal insomnia
    @reveal racing-thoughts-night
    @set admitted_sleep_issues = true
    
@elseif rapport >= 40
    PATIENT (hesitant)
    "It's... complicated."
    
    PATIENT
    "Some nights are better than others. I [do sleep]. Just not 
    always when I want to."
    
    @pause 0.5
    
    PATIENT (hedging)
    "My mind has trouble [settling down] sometimes. But that's 
    probably normal?"
    
    PATIENT (seeking validation)
    "Everyone has nights like that. Don't they?"
    
    @rapport +5
    
@else
    PATIENT (defensive)
    "I mentioned this already—my sleep is [fine]<contradicts:bags-under-eyes>."
    
    PATIENT
    "I mean, not perfect. But I don't think I need sleep medication or 
    anything like that."
    
    PATIENT (nervous)
    "Unless you think I do? But I really don't think that's the issue."
    
    @rapport +1
@endif

=== @response:sleep.routine ===
@if rapport >= 50
    PATIENT (thoughtful)
    "Routine? I have one. A very [specific one], actually."
    
    @pause 0.5
    
    PATIENT
    "I check that everything is locked. Usually [multiple times]. Then I 
    check my phone for any emails I might have missed."
    
    PATIENT (anxious)
    "Then I lie down and... try to sleep. But my mind starts going 
    through everything that happened. Everything that might happen 
    tomorrow."
    
    PATIENT (frustrated)
    "The routine doesn't seem to [help]. I've tried chamomile tea. 
    White noise. Everything the articles suggest."
    
    @pause 1
    
    PATIENT (vulnerable)
    "Sometimes I just stay up and [triple-check my work for the next day]. 
    At least then I feel like I'm being productive."
    
    @rapport +8
    @reveal compulsive-checking
    @reveal avoidance-behavior
    
@else
    PATIENT (guarded)
    "I have a routine. Go to bed at a reasonable hour. Wake up at a 
    reasonable hour."
    
    PATIENT (hedging)
    "It works. Mostly."
    
    @rapport +2
@endif

=== @response:sleep.thoughts ===
@if rapport >= 65
    PATIENT (vulnerable)
    "What goes through my mind?"
    
    @pause 1.5
    
    PATIENT (anxious)
    "Everything. [Everything I did wrong that day]."
    
    PATIENT
    "That thing I said in the meeting—did it come across as stupid? 
    That email I sent—was the tone right?"
    
    PATIENT (distressed)
    "People's faces. The way someone looked at me. Did they notice 
    something? Were they judging me?"
    
    @pause 1
    
    PATIENT (sad)
    "And then the bigger things. What if I'm [not good enough]? What if 
    people figure out that I'm just... pretending to have it together?"
    
    PATIENT (quietly)
    "Some nights I convince myself everyone can see right through me."
    
    @rapport +15
    @reveal fear-of-judgment
    @reveal impostor-feelings
    @reveal racing-thoughts-detail
    
@else
    PATIENT (guarded)
    "Just... thoughts. Normal things."
    
    PATIENT
    "Work stuff, mostly. Things I need to do."
    
    @rapport +2
@endif

// -------------------------------------------
// SOCIAL - Relationships and Interactions
// -------------------------------------------

=== @response:social.friends ===
@if rapport >= 50
    PATIENT (hesitant)
    "My social life..."
    
    @pause 1
    
    PATIENT (sad)
    "I have friends. I [think] I have friends. People I know."
    
    PATIENT
    "But I don't see them as often as I probably should. It's 
    [exhausting], somehow."
    
    PATIENT (thoughtful)
    "Being around people requires so much... management. Making sure 
    I'm saying the right things. Laughing at the right moments."
    
    @pause 0.5
    
    PATIENT (vulnerable)
    "Afterwards I'm [drained]. And then I spend the rest of the night 
    analyzing everything I said."
    
    @rapport +8
    @reveal social-exhaustion
    
@else
    PATIENT (guarded)
    "I have friends. We see each other sometimes."
    
    PATIENT
    "I've been busy lately, so maybe not as much as I should."
    
    @rapport +2
@endif

=== @response:social.interactions ===
@if rapport >= 55
    PATIENT (nervous)
    "How do I feel around others?"
    
    @pause 1
    
    PATIENT (anxious)
    "Like I'm [constantly being watched]. Evaluated."
    
    PATIENT
    "I'm always aware of how I'm standing. Whether my posture looks 
    confident enough. Whether my voice sounds normal."
    
    PATIENT (vulnerable)
    "It's like there's this [running commentary] in my head. 'Don't 
    fidget. Make eye contact. Not too much eye contact. Say something 
    intelligent.'"
    
    @pause 0.5
    
    PATIENT (exhausted)
    "It never stops. Even now. [Especially now]."
    
    @rapport +10
    @reveal hypervigilance-social
    @reveal self-monitoring
    
@else
    PATIENT (guarded)
    "Fine. Normal, I think."
    
    PATIENT (hedging)
    "Maybe a little self-conscious sometimes. But everyone is, right?"
    
    @rapport +2
@endif

=== @response:social.avoidance ===
@if rapport >= 60
    PATIENT (defensive at first)
    "I don't... avoid things."
    
    @pause 1
    
    PATIENT (reconsidering)
    "Well. Maybe I [avoid some things]."
    
    PATIENT
    "Large gatherings. Places where I might run into people unexpectedly. 
    Situations where I haven't had time to [prepare what to say]."
    
    PATIENT (vulnerable)
    "I tell myself I'm just an introvert. But sometimes I wonder if it's 
    more than that."
    
    @pause 0.5
    
    PATIENT (quietly)
    "I've turned down job promotions because they involved more 
    [public speaking]. More visibility."
    
    @rapport +12
    @reveal avoidance-pattern
    @reveal career-impact
    
@else
    PATIENT (defensive)
    "I don't avoid things. I'm just... selective about how I spend 
    my energy."
    
    @rapport +1
@endif

// -------------------------------------------
// EMOTIONS - Feelings and Inner Experience
// -------------------------------------------

=== @response:emotions.general ===
@if rapport >= 45
    PATIENT (thoughtful)
    "How have I been feeling..."
    
    @pause 1
    
    PATIENT (hesitant)
    "On edge, I suppose. Like I'm [waiting for something to go wrong]."
    
    PATIENT
    "Even when things are going well, I can't enjoy it. Because I'm 
    thinking about what might happen next."
    
    PATIENT (sad)
    "I'm tired. [Really tired]. But also too wound up to rest."
    
    @pause 0.5
    
    PATIENT (vulnerable)
    "Does that make sense? I feel like I'm not explaining this right."
    
    @rapport +8
    @reveal anticipatory-anxiety
    
@else
    PATIENT (guarded)
    "I've been fine. Functional."
    
    PATIENT (hedging)
    "A bit stressed maybe. But who isn't?"
    
    @rapport +2
@endif

=== @response:emotions.worry ===
@if rapport >= 55
    PATIENT (anxious)
    "What do I worry about?"
    
    @pause 0.5
    
    PATIENT (overwhelmed)
    "[Everything]. Genuinely, everything."
    
    PATIENT
    "Big things—my career, my health, whether I'm where I should be 
    at my age."
    
    PATIENT (frustrated)
    "And tiny things. Did I lock the door? Did I turn off the stove? 
    Did that email sound professional enough?"
    
    @pause 1
    
    PATIENT (vulnerable)
    "I check things [over and over]. And even after I check, part of 
    me isn't sure. What if I missed something?"
    
    PATIENT (quietly)
    "It's exhausting. Living like this."
    
    @rapport +12
    @reveal chronic-worry
    @reveal checking-behavior
    
@else
    PATIENT (guarded)
    "Normal things. Work. Responsibilities."
    
    PATIENT (hedging)
    "Nothing unusual, I don't think."
    
    @rapport +2
@endif

=== @response:emotions.calm ===
@if rapport >= 55
    PATIENT (thoughtful)
    "When do I feel most at ease?"
    
    @pause 1.5
    
    PATIENT (sad)
    "I'm not sure I remember what that feels like."
    
    PATIENT (hesitant)
    "Maybe... alone? When I can just... [stop performing]."
    
    PATIENT
    "When no one is watching. When I don't have to worry about how 
    I'm coming across."
    
    @pause 0.5
    
    PATIENT (vulnerable)
    "But even then, my mind doesn't really [quiet down]. It just 
    finds other things to worry about."
    
    @rapport +8
    @reveal no-respite
    @reveal always-performing
    
@else
    PATIENT (guarded)
    "When things are... under control. When I've prepared properly."
    
    @rapport +2
@endif

// -------------------------------------------
// APPEARANCE - Self-Presentation
// -------------------------------------------

=== @response:appearance.presentation ===
NARRATOR
*Gregory's hand moves self-consciously to straighten his collar, which 
was already perfectly straight.*

@pause 0.5

@if rapport >= 55
    PATIENT (nervous)
    "Put-together?"
    
    PATIENT
    "I... try to be. It takes [quite a bit of effort], actually."
    
    @pause 0.5
    
    PATIENT (vulnerable)
    "I'm very aware of how I look. How I might be [perceived]."
    
    PATIENT
    "If there's a wrinkle. If a hair is out of place. These things 
    feel... important."
    
    PATIENT (hesitant)
    "I know that probably sounds shallow. But if I look put-together, 
    maybe people won't notice that I [don't feel put-together]."
    
    @rapport +10
    @reveal appearance-as-armor
    @reveal disconnect-inside-outside
    
@else
    PATIENT (guarded)
    "Thank you. I try to present myself [professionally]."
    
    @rapport +2
@endif

=== @response:appearance.effort ===
@if rapport >= 60
    PATIENT (hesitant)
    "How much effort?"
    
    @pause 1
    
    PATIENT (embarrassed)
    "More than I'd like to admit."
    
    PATIENT
    "I check myself in mirrors constantly. Bathroom mirrors, car 
    mirrors, my phone's camera."
    
    PATIENT (anxious)
    "What if something is wrong and I don't know? What if everyone 
    can see something I can't?"
    
    @pause 0.5
    
    PATIENT (vulnerable)
    "I spent [twenty minutes] this morning making sure my hair was 
    right. Twenty minutes, and I still wasn't sure."
    
    @rapport +12
    @reveal appearance-anxiety
    @reveal time-spent-appearance
    
@else
    PATIENT (guarded)
    "A reasonable amount. I believe in presenting myself well."
    
    @rapport +2
@endif

=== @response:appearance.judgment ===
@if rapport >= 65
    PATIENT (vulnerable)
    "Do I worry about how others see me?"
    
    @pause 1.5
    
    PATIENT (quietly)
    "Constantly. [Every moment]."
    
    PATIENT (anxious)
    "I can feel eyes on me. Even when there probably aren't any. 
    People looking. Noticing."
    
    PATIENT
    "Noticing that my nails are bitten. That I look tired. That I'm 
    not as [together as I'm pretending to be]."
    
    @pause 1
    
    PATIENT (sad)
    "I try so hard to be... correct. To not stand out. But I'm 
    [six foot one with red hair]. I always stand out."
    
    PATIENT (vulnerable)
    "I can never just... blend in. Be invisible."
    
    @rapport +15
    @reveal fear-of-judgment
    @reveal standing-out
    @reveal desire-to-disappear
    
@else
    PATIENT (defensive)
    "I think everyone cares about how they're perceived."
    
    PATIENT
    "That's just being self-aware, isn't it?"
    
    @rapport +1
@endif

// -------------------------------------------
// SELF - Identity and Self-Perception
// -------------------------------------------

=== @response:self.identity ===
@if rapport >= 60
    PATIENT (thoughtful)
    "How would I describe myself..."
    
    @pause 1.5
    
    PATIENT (hesitant)
    "I don't know. I [genuinely don't know]."
    
    PATIENT
    "I know what I want people to see. Competent. Put-together. 
    Reliable."
    
    PATIENT (vulnerable)
    "But underneath that... I'm not sure there's anything [solid]."
    
    @pause 0.5
    
    PATIENT (sad)
    "Just... worry. Constant worry. And this [exhausting performance] 
    of being okay."
    
    @rapport +12
    @reveal identity-uncertainty
    @reveal performing-normal
    
@else
    PATIENT (guarded)
    "Responsible. Detail-oriented. I try to do things correctly."
    
    @rapport +2
@endif

=== @response:self.expectations ===
@if rapport >= 65
    PATIENT (anxious)
    "What do I expect of myself?"
    
    @pause 1
    
    PATIENT (intense)
    "[Perfection]. Nothing less than perfection."
    
    PATIENT
    "Every email has to be worded exactly right. Every interaction 
    has to go smoothly. Every appearance has to be [flawless]."
    
    PATIENT (frustrated)
    "I know that's impossible. I [know] that. But the standard is 
    there anyway."
    
    @pause 0.5
    
    PATIENT (vulnerable)
    "And every time I fall short—which is always—I feel like I've 
    failed. Like everyone can see that I'm [not good enough]."
    
    @rapport +15
    @reveal perfectionism-core
    @reveal self-criticism
    
@else
    PATIENT (guarded)
    "I expect myself to meet my responsibilities. Do things properly."
    
    @rapport +2
@endif

=== @response:self.confidence ===
@if rapport >= 70
    PATIENT (sad)
    "Confident in my own judgment?"
    
    @pause 1.5
    
    PATIENT (quietly)
    "Not at all. [Not even a little]."
    
    PATIENT
    "I second-guess everything. Every decision. Every word I say."
    
    PATIENT (vulnerable)
    "That's why I keep asking you if I'm [doing this right]. If my 
    reasons for being here are [valid]. If my experiences are [normal]."
    
    @pause 0.5
    
    PATIENT (desperate)
    "I need someone else to tell me. Because I genuinely don't 
    [trust my own perception anymore]."
    
    @rapport +18
    @reveal deep-self-doubt
    @reveal reassurance-pattern
    @set breakthrough_potential = true
    
@else
    PATIENT (guarded)
    "Reasonably confident. I think."
    
    PATIENT (hedging)
    "Though I do like to get a second opinion when possible."
    
    @rapport +2
@endif

// -------------------------------------------
// WORK - Career and Daily Life
// -------------------------------------------

=== @response:work.job ===
@if rapport >= 35
    PATIENT
    "I work in [redacted for now]. Administrative work, mostly."
    
    PATIENT
    "It's... fine. Stable. The kind of job where attention to detail 
    matters."
    
    @pause 0.5
    
    PATIENT (thoughtful)
    "Maybe [too much] attention to detail sometimes. I tend to 
    check things over. Multiple times."
    
    @rapport +3
    
@else
    PATIENT (guarded)
    "Office work. Nothing glamorous."
    
    @rapport +1
@endif

=== @response:work.performance ===
@if rapport >= 55
    PATIENT (anxious)
    "My performance..."
    
    @pause 1
    
    PATIENT
    "My reviews are good. [Objectively good]. But I never believe them."
    
    PATIENT (vulnerable)
    "I keep waiting for someone to realize I [don't know what I'm doing]. 
    That I've been faking competence this whole time."
    
    PATIENT
    "Every meeting, I'm sure this is the one where they figure it out. 
    Where everyone sees through me."
    
    @pause 0.5
    
    PATIENT (sad)
    "The good reviews almost make it worse. Because now I have 
    [expectations to live up to]."
    
    @rapport +12
    @reveal impostor-syndrome
    @reveal performance-anxiety
    
@else
    PATIENT (guarded)
    "I do my job. I try to be thorough."
    
    @rapport +2
@endif

=== @response:work.stress ===
@if rapport >= 50
    PATIENT (thoughtful)
    "Is work stressful?"
    
    @pause 0.5
    
    PATIENT (honest)
    "Yes. But probably not in the way you'd expect."
    
    PATIENT
    "The work itself isn't hard. It's everything [around] the work."
    
    PATIENT (anxious)
    "Meetings. Interactions with colleagues. Making sure my emails 
    sound professional but not cold. Friendly but not unprofessional."
    
    @pause 1
    
    PATIENT (exhausted)
    "I spend more energy [managing how I come across] than I do 
    actually working."
    
    @rapport +8
    @reveal social-stress-work
    
@else
    PATIENT (guarded)
    "Work is work. Some days are more demanding than others."
    
    @rapport +2
@endif

// -------------------------------------------
// FAMILY - Background and History
// -------------------------------------------

=== @response:family.background ===
@if rapport >= 55
    PATIENT (hesitant)
    "My family..."
    
    @pause 1
    
    PATIENT
    "They're fine. [Good people]. We're not estranged or anything."
    
    PATIENT (thoughtful)
    "They had... high expectations. For how things should be done. 
    How I should behave."
    
    @pause 0.5
    
    PATIENT (quietly)
    "I learned early that the best way to avoid criticism was to be 
    [perfect]. Or at least to appear perfect."
    
    @rapport +8
    @reveal family-expectations
    
@else
    PATIENT (guarded)
    "Normal family. Nothing remarkable."
    
    @rapport +2
@endif

=== @response:family.childhood ===
@if rapport >= 65
    PATIENT (thoughtful)
    "Growing up..."
    
    @pause 1.5
    
    PATIENT (vulnerable)
    "I was always careful. [Always watching]."
    
    PATIENT
    "Making sure I was behaving correctly. That I wasn't doing 
    anything that would draw negative attention."
    
    PATIENT (sad)
    "I remember being [terrified of making mistakes]. Because 
    mistakes meant disappointment. Correction."
    
    @pause 0.5
    
    PATIENT (quietly)
    "I think I've been performing [my whole life]. I just didn't 
    realize it wasn't supposed to feel this exhausting."
    
    @rapport +15
    @reveal childhood-anxiety
    @reveal lifelong-performance
    
@else
    PATIENT (guarded)
    "It was fine. Normal childhood."
    
    @rapport +2
@endif

=== @response:family.expectations ===
@if rapport >= 70
    PATIENT (nervous)
    "What did they expect?"
    
    @pause 1
    
    PATIENT (intense)
    "[Everything to be done correctly]. Always."
    
    PATIENT
    "Good grades. Good behavior. Good appearance. No mistakes. 
    No complaints."
    
    PATIENT (vulnerable)
    "I learned that my feelings didn't matter as much as how 
    things looked. How I came across."
    
    @pause 1
    
    PATIENT (sad)
    "I'm still doing it. [Still trying to be correct]. Still 
    unsure if I'm allowed to just... be."
    
    @rapport +18
    @reveal perfectionism-origin
    @reveal invalidation-history
    @set family_breakthrough = true
    
@else
    PATIENT (guarded)
    "They wanted me to do well. Be successful."
    
    PATIENT
    "Normal parental expectations, I suppose."
    
    @rapport +2
@endif

